{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789342935,"nonce":"mEtmdVOqYg7OwCfq/0jtMNWbF3I=","title":"Two compiles of one source produce differently ordered HIR","message":"`rebuild_cfg_edges` (in inline and licm) builds predecessor lists by\niterating a HashMap of successors, and `pure_call_pre` applies its hoist\nplans in HashMap order, so the values it mints land in `func.values` in\nan order that changes from run to run. The canonical dump names values\nand blocks by position, so the same function fingerprints differently\nacross two compiles and a hot reload of unchanged source reports it as\nchanged.\n\nSeen once recursive self-inlining ran two rounds: `hot_reload_call_boundary`\n(`reloading_the_same_source_is_a_noop`, `a_formatting_only_edit_reloads_nothing`)\nreported `f` reloaded. One round left too few PRE groups for the order\nto show.\n\nFix: predecessor lists follow block order; PRE groups are handled in the\norder their first site appears. Other passes that iterate HashMaps while\ncreating values would show the same way; the fingerprint tests are the\ndetector.","files":null}]}